course: dictionary
lesson: 6474
title: A naturalist looks closely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A naturalist is a person who studies plants, animals and nature. The clue is in the word: naturalist sounds like nature, and a naturalist learns about nature by watching it carefully, often outside in the wild. «Science about living things starts with looking very carefully.»
explain: Context helps here too. «So read the Wild Wood like a naturalist: enjoy the story, then ask what the real animal would be doing.» A naturalist notices real animals and asks how they live, not just what happens in a story.
explain: You can be a naturalist too, even at your age. «A girl in the park who draws a beetle in her notebook, writes the date and counts its legs is doing what naturalists have always done.» An amateur naturalist does this for the love of nature, not as a job.
fact: A naturalist is a person who studies plants, animals and nature, often by watching them carefully in the wild.
fact: A less common meaning: a writer or artist who shows life exactly as it is.
fact: Charles Darwin and David Attenborough are famous naturalists who observed living things closely.
fact: Around 1799 the naturalist George Shaw checked the first platypus skin for stitches.
fact: You can be a young naturalist by keeping a nature diary, pond dipping or bird watching.
exercise: «Science about living things starts with looking very carefully.» What does a naturalist do? | Writes a story about a dragon | Sells pets in a shop | Sleeps through the summer holidays | *Studies plants and animals by watching them closely
exercise: «A girl in the park who draws a beetle in her notebook» is like a naturalist because she | Buys a new notebook for school | Plays football with her friends | Hides from the beetle | *Watches a beetle closely and records what she sees
exercise: Which two people are named as famous naturalists in the lessons? | Nadia and Jayden | Ella and Leo | Shakespeare and Dickens | *Charles Darwin and David Attenborough
test: What does a keen naturalist do for fun? | Only reads comics | Collects coins | Plays video games all day | *Notices birds, insects and plants and wonders how they live
test: Why should you read the Wild Wood like a naturalist? | To find the pages with pictures only | *To ask what a real animal would be doing | To guess the last page first | To skip the story entirely
exam: The less common meaning of naturalist is a writer or artist who shows life exactly as it is. What does this mean? | *A writer or artist who shows life as it really is | A teacher who checks homework | A doctor who studies bones | Someone who paints houses
